62 140.22972 485.7516 140.22972 \nL 407.1852 140.22972 \nQ 402.2748 140.22972 402.2748 142.5582 \nL 402.2748 204.26292 \nQ 402.2748 206.5914 407.1852 206.5914 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6a8a226bb0)\" style=\"fill: #eef3f9; stroke: #9ab0c8; stroke-linejoin: miter\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_20\">\n    <path d=\"M 446.22288 100.296288 \nQ 446.22288 110.075904 446.22288 119.85552 \n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6a8a226bb0)\" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #0b2a5a; stroke-width: 1.2; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_21\">\n    <path d=\"M 53.39088 119.85552 \nQ 53.39088 129.402288 53.39088 137.607415 \n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6a8a226bb0)\" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #0b2a5a; stroke-width: 1.2; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 55.19088 134.007415 \nL 53.39088 137.607415 \nL 51.59088 134.007415 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6a8a226bb0)\" style=\"fill: #0b2a5a; stroke: #0b2a5a; stroke-width: 1.2; stroke-linecap: round\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"line2d_1\">\n    <path d=\"M 446.22288 98.8992 \nL 484.524 112.87008 \nL 484.524 119.85552 \n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6a8a226bb0)\" style=\"fill: none\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"line2d_2\">\n    <path d=\"M 53.39088 119.85552 \nL 446.22288 119.85552 \n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6a8a226bb0)\" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #0b2a5a; stroke-width: 1.2; stroke-linecap: square\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_1\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(27.032525 62.34354)\">Decide scope</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(25.455947 75.432389)\">and who leads</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_2\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(119.725384 56.084834)\">Gap assessment</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(130.495572 68.496543)\">against the</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(134.795447 81.633439)\">standard</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_3\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(219.916759 49.835737)\">Close the gaps:</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(222.909759 62.385821)\">fix processes,</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(220.476666 74.729624)\">write only what</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(232.079025 87.033708)\">you need</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_4\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(318.397666 56.028459)\">Run the system</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(314.453338 68.446574)\">and keep records</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(319.069681 81.77758)\">for 2–3 months</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_5\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(421.203431 56.927255)\">Internal audit</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(412.811884 68.398527)\">and management</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(433.714197 81.735298)\">review</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_6\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(28.892259 163.204523)\">Stage 1 audit</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(26.395744 176.439435)\">readiness and</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(32.031322 188.747363)\">documents</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_7\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(126.267447 163.204523)\">Stage 2 audit</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(130.619853 175.540638)\">the system</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(140.297775 188.845378)\">in use</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_8\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(229.838119 170.280666)\">Certificate</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(225.465853 181.839704)\">valid 3 years</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_9\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(324.548306 164.037335)\">Surveillance</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(331.996213 176.439435)\">audits in</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(322.733416 187.983097)\">years 1 and 2</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_10\">\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(418.414791 170.280666)\">Recertification</text>\n    <text style=\"font-size: 8.2px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; fill: #0b2a5a\" transform=\"translate(418.989431 181.839704)\">audit in year 3</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_11\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 9.5px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: start; fill: #0b6fa4\" x=\"10.6704\" y=\"23.186691\" transform=\"rotate(-0 10.6704 23.186691)\">Your preparation</text>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_12\">\n    <text style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 9.5px; font-family: 'Inter', 'DejaVu Sans'; text-anchor: start; fill: #4d7f12\" x=\"10.6704\" y=\"228.092931\" transform=\"rotate(-0 10.6704 228.092931)\">Certification body</text>\n   </g>\n  </g>\n </g>\n <defs>\n  <clipPath id=\"p6a8a226bb0\">\n   <rect x=\"5.76\" y=\"5.76\" width=\"491.04\" height=\"232.848\"/>\n  </clipPath>\n </defs>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>The path to certification and the three-year cycle that follows.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Certification is carried out by an independent certification body. In Canada, look for one accredited by the Standards Council of Canada or by another accreditation body recognized internationally, because customers may not accept a certificate from a body that is not accredited. The audit has two stages. Stage 1 checks that the system is designed and ready. Stage 2 checks that it is in use and effective. The certificate is valid for three years, with a shorter surveillance audit each year and a recertification audit in the third year.</p>\n<p>Build to ISO 9001:2026. It was published in September 2026 and replaces the 2015 edition; <a href=\"post/iso-9001-2026-what-changed-from-2015.html\">this article explains what changed</a>.</p>\n<h2>How long it takes and what drives the cost</h2>\n<p>For a business with fewer than 50 people and reasonably orderly operations, six to nine months from decision to certificate is a realistic plan. Most of that time is spent running the system and collecting records, since an auditor needs to see it working over a period.</p>\n<p>There are three kinds of cost. The certification body's fees depend mainly on headcount, the number of sites and the complexity of what you do, so ask two or three accredited bodies for quotes. Internal time is usually the largest cost, mostly from the person leading the project and from process owners. Outside help is optional. It is worth paying for a gap assessment, internal auditor training and a pre-audit check; it is rarely worth paying someone to write your system for you, because a system written by an outsider tends to describe a company that does not exist.</p>\n<h2>A lean way to build it</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Define the scope.</strong> State which products, services and sites the certificate will cover.</li>\n<li><strong>Map your main processes on one page.</strong> From enquiry to delivery, with the support processes around them. Name an owner for each.</li>\n<li><strong>Compare with the standard.</strong> Note where you already meet a requirement and where you do not. Most businesses find they meet more than they expected.</li>\n<li><strong>Close the gaps with the lightest fix.</strong> A checklist, a form or a short visual instruction is often better than a procedure.</li>\n<li><strong>Set three to five objectives you already care about.</strong> On-time delivery, complaints, scrap or rework are common choices.</li>\n<li><strong>Run it and keep records.</strong> Two to three months of evidence is typical before the stage 2 audit.</li>\n<li><strong>Audit yourself and hold a management review.</strong> See <a href=\"post/iso-9001-internal-audits-that-find-real-problems.html\">internal audits that find real problems</a> and <a href=\"post/iso-9001-management-review-that-leadership-finds-useful.html\">management review that leadership finds useful</a>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Is it worth it?</h2>\n<p>If a customer requires the certificate, the commercial answer is simple. The longer-term value depends on how the system is built. A system that describes how you really work gives you clearer responsibilities, fewer repeated problems and a regular, fact-based review of the business. A system built only to pass the audit gives you a certificate and an annual chore. The standard is the same in both cases. The difference is in the choices you make while building it.</p>\n<p><strong>Want a second pair of eyes?</strong> Chmltech helps Canadian organizations build, simplify and audit quality management systems. <a href=\"../book.html\">Book a strategy call</a> or <a href=\"../contact.html\">ask a question</a>.</p>\n<h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.iso.org/quality-management/iso-9001-2026\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">ISO: ISO 9001:2026, what businesses need to know</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.dqsglobal.com/en/explore/blog/iso-9001-2026-changes-timeline-transition\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">DQS: ISO 9001:2026, key changes, timeline and transition checklist</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.sgs.com/en-gb/showcases/iso-9001-2026-key-updates-and-transition-guidance\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">SGS: ISO 9001:2026 key updates and transition guidance</a></li></ul>\n<h2>More in this series</h2><ul><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-2026-what-changed-from-2015.html\">ISO 9001:2026: what changed from 2015</a></li><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-2026-transition-plan.html\">Your ISO 9001:2026 transition plan</a></li><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-internal-audits-that-find-real-problems.html\">Internal audits that find real problems</a></li><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-risk-based-thinking-in-practice.html\">Risk-based thinking in practice</a></li><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-and-ai-using-ai-tools-inside-a-quality-system.html\">ISO 9001 and AI</a></li><li><a href=\"post/integrated-management-system-iso-9001-14001-45001.html\">Integrating ISO 9001, ISO 14001 and ISO 45001</a></li><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-management-review-that-leadership-finds-useful.html\">Management review that leadership finds useful</a></li><li><a href=\"post/iso-9001-document-and-revision-control.html\">Document and revision control</a></li></ul>",
